<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46975" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sup-plōdo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subpl-</span></b> ), or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sup-plaudo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subpl-</span></b> ), si, 3, v. a. and
		n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to
				stamp</i> the foot: pedem nemo in illo judicio supplosit,
			* <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 1, 53, 230</span></i>; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pedem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 75, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>To clap</i> in token of applause, <i>to applaud</i> (eccl. Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">male nobis supplaudimus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Idol. 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">diversae parti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Pud. 19</span></i>
			. — * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>To tread under foot</i>, <i>to
			destroy</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calumniam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. Somn. Scip. 1, 2, §
				3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
